# Agent behaviour

- On a **new machine / 3090 clone**: execute root `HANDOFF.md` first, then `AGENTS.md`.
  On this 4090 tree: read `AGENTS.md` → `docs/STATUS.md` → top of `progress.md` before acting.
  Do not jump ahead of the plan; do not write "done" for anything whose `result.json` is not on disk.
- Four living documents, and when to touch them: `AGENTS.md` only when a rule/contract/long-term fact changes;
  `docs/STATUS.md` whenever job state, cell counts, next steps or the countdown change (update it before ending
  a session); `progress.md` one dated entry per substantive action (newest on top); `docs/DECISIONS.md` one
  numbered entry per decision that changes numbers, protocol or wording. No FILE_CATALOG / operation_log mirrors.
- Never fabricate results. Never peek at test metrics to choose the main model (pre-registration in
  `docs/PLAN_spiking_eegnex_icassp2027.md` §0.3 rules).
- Reports follow: core conclusion → goal → method → protocol → results → analysis → relation to prior work →
  next step → file list. Markdown under root and `docs/` carries YAML frontmatter; snake_case filenames.
- Everything the senior needs to see goes to `docs/reports/` as a dated file; do not leave knowledge only in chat.
- Keep `SYX/` top level clean: ICASSP material only in this directory, benchmark material only in `../Benchmark`.
